.TH MS 1 "December 2025" "ms 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ms \- Python-based 'ls' replacement with advanced features
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ms
[\fI\-a\fR] [\fI\-l\fR] [\fI\-L\fR] [\fI\-H\fR] [\fI\-t\fR] [\fI\-T\fR] [\fI\-M\fR] [\fI--sort\fR \fIname|type|date\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ms
is a Python-based replacement for the Unix
.B ls
command, with additional features like tree view, colorized output, human-readable file sizes, and sorting options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show hidden files (those starting with a dot).
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-long
Use a long listing format, showing permissions, size, and modification time.
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-long-zebra
Use a long listing format with zebra-styled rows for better readability.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-human
Display file sizes in human-readable format in two rows, with colorized types.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-tree
Display directories and files in a tree-like structure (full tree).
.TP
.B \-T, \-\-tree-folders
Display only folders in a tree-like structure.
.TP
.B \-M, \-\-tree-metadata
Display directories and files in a tree-like structure with metadata (size, modification time).
.TP
.B \-\-sort \fIname|type|date\fR
Sort files by name (default), type, or modification date.
.TP
.B path
The directory to list. Defaults to the current directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ms
List files in the current directory.
.TP
.B ms \-l
List files in long format.
.TP
.B ms \-L
List files in long format with zebra-styled rows.
.TP
.B ms \-H
List files with human-readable sizes in two rows.
.TP
.B ms \-t
List files and directories in a full tree view.
.TP
.B ms \-T
List only folders in a tree view.
.TP
.B ms \-M
List files and directories in a tree view with metadata.
.TP
.B ms --sort type
List files sorted by type.
.TP
.B ms /path/to/dir
List files in the specified directory.
